    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="1005" n="987" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg987"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.51/10–1047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-10T12:00:00+01:00">October 10,
                            1947—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5466. ReDeptel 4217 [<hi rendition="#italic">4207</hi>], September 30, to London,
                    repeated Rome 1884.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d655-f1"/> Fortezza<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d655-f2"/> protocol signed on schedule 11 a. m. London time by
                    Gallman for US, Bevin for UK and Italian Chargé B. Migone.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d655-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Text follows that quoted Embstel 5353, October 3, repeated Rome 120, Paris 5361,
                    October 4, repeated Paris 555, Rome 121, October 6 and Embstel 5391, October 7,
                    repeated Paris 559, Rome 123. US copy being forwarded cover air despatch
                        immediately.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d655-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department 5466; repeated Paris 562; Rome 128.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gallman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d655-f1" n="1" xml:id="d655-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d655-f2" n="2" xml:id="d655-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 1442, May 29, 1945, from Rome, not printed, Ambassador Kirk reported
                    that the gold discovered by U.S. troops at Fortezza, valued at approximately $25
                    million, had been identified as a portion of the gold reserve of the Bank of
                    Italy, apparently removed to northern Italy by the Fascist Republican
                    government. (865.515/5–2945) In the memorandum by Ness of June 3 (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg913">p. 913</ref>), the value
                    of the gold was estimated at $28 million. For additional information, see
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, October 19, 1947, p.
                    770.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d655-f3" n="3" xml:id="d655-f3-content">
                <p>Bartolomeo Migone.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d655-f4" n="4" xml:id="d655-f4-content">
                <p>None printed; for text of the Protocol, “Transfer to Italian Government of Gold
                    Captured at Fortezza”, see Department of State Treaties and Other International
                    Acts Series (TIAS) No. 1658, or 61 Stat. (pt.
                    3) 3239.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
